  "worked_solution": "Since the given series is in the form ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{N}a{r}^{n},$ it is a geometric series. \n\nTo determine the sum, we use the formula for the sum ${S}_{N}$ of a geometric series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}={a}_{1}\\frac{(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $r=8$ and $N=5.$ We need to figure out the value of ${a}_{1}.$\n\nThe formula for the $n$th term of the series is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{3}{4}(8)^{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore we can calculate the first term ${a}_{1}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =\\frac{3}{4}(8)^{1} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we substitute ${a}_{1}=6,r=8$ and $N=5$ into the formula for ${S}_{N}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{5}\\frac{3}{4}(8)^{n} & =6\\cdot \\frac{(1-{8}^{5})}{1-8} \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{(1-{8}^{5})}{(-7)} \\\\  & =6(\\frac{-32\\,767}{-7}) \\\\  & =28\\,086\\end{aligned}\n$$",
